1
00:00:05,240 --> 00:00:06,160
YAMU!

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:09,000
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

3
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,618
You're on the move!

4
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:09,877
The KC Grand Championship
is heating up after

5
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:12,431
some incredible duels and stunning upsets.

6
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:16,394
We're moving into the semi-finals
where Rebecca Hawkins,

7
00:01:16,580 --> 00:01:18,600
Balbrey Ginger, Leon Wilson,

8
00:01:18,820 --> 00:01:22,157
and Siegfried Lloyd will
duke it out for a title

9
00:01:22,240 --> 00:01:25,500
shot against the international
Duel Monsters champion,

10
00:01:25,940 --> 00:01:27,080
Yugi Moto! No!

11
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:29,980
Pardon me, sir.

12
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:33,837
As you requested, we've conducted
an in-depth investigation of Mr.

13
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:34,797
Siegfried Lloyd.

14
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:36,180
This better be good.

15
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:39,217
It appears Siegfried
has participated in over

16
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:41,737
50 tournaments in the
last three years alone,

17
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:43,820
each time ranking in the top five.

18
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,157
But our research revealed almost nothing

19
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:49,828
about personal background
or family history,

20
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:54,137
and there's no record of any connection
with that Schroeder family you mentioned.

21
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:57,537
So this Siegfried has been winning
tournaments around the world,

22
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:59,738
and no one knows anything about him?

23
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:01,090
Apparently,

24
00:02:01,173 --> 00:02:03,177
he gains entry into these
tournaments by receiving

25
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,137
letters of recommendation
from local politicians.

26
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:07,400
Yeah, like who?

27
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:12,505
I have compiled a list with dozens of
names, but none were available for comment.

28
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:15,440
They just need some incentive.

29
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,292
Let me take a look at this list of yours.

30
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:19,850
Yes, sir.

31
00:02:19,933 --> 00:02:22,480
He has some powerful people in his corner.

32
00:02:24,100 --> 00:02:25,140
Number 13

33
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,600
Question that man again

34
00:02:29,140 --> 00:02:32,677
And if he still refuses
to make a comment I want

35
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:35,937
you to make him an offer
he can't refuse Yes, Mr.

36
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:36,850
Kaiba

37
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:42,100
I've got you by the tail, you rat

38
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,620
Oh man, Joey lost

39
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,440
Hold on a sec.

40
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:54,870
Awesome!

41
00:02:54,953 --> 00:02:58,800
That means Yugi can cheer
for me from now on! Yes!

42
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:09,089
I was knocked out of the
tournament by a guy with pink hair.

43
00:03:09,340 --> 00:03:12,480
Yeah, a guy with pink hair
who's an expert duelist.

44
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:14,680
I want to be number one!

45
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,560
Oh, well, you grow up.

46
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,057
Trust me, there'll be other duels.

47
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:21,957
You're not the one who's
a runner-up every year.

48
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,780
That honor belongs to me.

49
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
He's got a point.

50
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:26,535
Think of it this way.

51
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:30,717
In the end, every match you lose
just helps make you a better duelist.

52
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,800
Then he should be the best by now.

53
00:03:33,020 --> 00:03:33,850
Hey!

54
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,137
Yugi, it's your grandfather.

55
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:38,050
What's wrong?

56
00:03:38,420 --> 00:03:39,300
Where is he?

57
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:43,737
Yeah, did he ever make it to the medical
center after he threw his back out?

58
00:03:43,820 --> 00:03:45,020
He was there.

59
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,820
Oi, my back!

60
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,120
The pain!

61
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:53,890
I'll get the doctor.

62
00:03:53,973 --> 00:03:58,800
In the meanwhile, try not to
move. Dr. Grossfeld? Hello?

63
00:04:01,820 --> 00:04:03,020
Where'd he go?

64
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,320
Rebecca's duel! Now! Attack!

65
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,560
I haven't missed it! Come on!

66
00:04:11,460 --> 00:04:12,290
Yes!

67
00:04:12,540 --> 00:04:13,980
Now finish him off!

68
00:04:14,320 --> 00:04:15,860
She's a true Hawkins!

69
00:04:16,140 --> 00:04:17,920
Oh yes, the doctor!

70
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:23,481
Let's have a look here, shall we?

71
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,814
It looks like your friend's been cured.

72
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,755
I'll send you a bill.

73
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:32,300
I just wish I hadn't been distracted.

74
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:33,902
Don't sweat it.

75
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,317
I'm sure Gramps is fine.

76
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:37,597
But he was barely able to move a muscle,

77
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:40,157
so he couldn't possibly
have gotten out of that bed.

78
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:42,360
Maybe someone came and helped him?

79
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:43,860
Yeah, but who?

80
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,320
Perhaps his secret admirer.

81
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:48,557
Could you be serious for once?

82
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,797
What, you saying Gramps is unattractive?

83
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,717
Come on, we need a plan, guys.

84
00:04:52,800 --> 00:04:54,380
He may be in real trouble.

85
00:04:54,720 --> 00:04:56,037
You got a point there, Duke.

86
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:58,767
He does have the worst
luck of anyone I know.

87
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,549
Let's just think positive.

88
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:05,040
I'm sure he's just
fine, pal. Me too. Yeah.

89
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:06,858
And his girlfriend.

90
00:05:07,740 --> 00:05:09,400
You're right. Thanks, guys.

91
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:10,840
Hey, no sweat.

92
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:14,775
Professor Hawkins, you should
go and cheer for Rebecca.

93
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,437
Yeah, we'll catch up later.

94
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:19,080
Just as soon as we find Yugi's grandpa.

95
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:20,880
Best of luck.

96
00:05:21,060 --> 00:05:21,900
And thanks.

97
00:05:22,780 --> 00:05:25,857
Tell Rebecca we're all rooting
for her and we'll see her soon.

98
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:26,770
Of course.

99
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:30,300
Guys, let's split up and
find that grandpa. Right!

100
00:05:34,660 --> 00:05:35,490
Huh?

101
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,680
Where is everyone?

102
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:42,120
I thought they'd be here
to cheer me on. Rebecca!

103
00:05:42,960 --> 00:05:43,790
Hey!

104
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:45,620
You made it!

105
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:49,080
Well done, Rebecca.

106
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:51,220
Now you're in the semi-finals.

107
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:55,620
Yep, but I thought Yugi would be
here to watch me. Where is he?

108
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:59,300
Well, he had to deal with a situation,

109
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:02,699
but I'm sure he'll come
back just as soon as he can.

110
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,340
Right now, you have a duel to focus on.

111
00:06:05,540 --> 00:06:06,420
But Gramps!

112
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,357
They'll all be here before
the match is through.

113
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,180
I promise. Okay.

114
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:15,331
Oh, and Yugi told me to tell
you that he's rooting for you.

115
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:16,670
Wait, he did?

116
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:19,540
I mean, those were his exact words? Yes.

117
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:21,744
Now let's go before we're late.

118
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,560
This is awesome.

119
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,353
For the first time in my life, I'm tall.

120
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,380
This place is so cute.

121
00:06:32,840 --> 00:06:35,760
It's just like our town,
only everything's mini.

122
00:06:36,560 --> 00:06:37,660
Except him.

123
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,471
The detail on these statues is incredible.

124
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,997
I must have dozed off.

125
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,420
And they speak, too.

126
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,060
That's Leon Wilson.

127
00:06:48,180 --> 00:06:50,040
I was up all night practicing.

128
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:52,280
I suppose I just needed a nap.

129
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,350
Figures.

130
00:06:54,580 --> 00:06:56,286
So when's Yugi gonna show up?

131
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:59,157
I was really hoping he
could watch my next duel.

132
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:02,064
He'll be here, but he's
gonna be rooting for me.

133
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,967
And what about your
friends and family, Leon?

134
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:06,258
Won't they be here?

135
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,037
Nah, everyone was too busy to come.

136
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:12,040
But I'm used to being on my own. Oh.

137
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,590
Eh.

138
00:07:13,673 --> 00:07:15,880
Well, not this time. Huh? Take a look.

139
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,360
Now you see what I mean?

140
00:07:29,580 --> 00:07:32,900
You two are surrounded by
fans who came to cheer you on.

141
00:07:33,140 --> 00:07:34,620
Now don't let them down!

142
00:07:41,480 --> 00:07:42,940
Yeah, you're right.

143
00:07:43,240 --> 00:07:45,617
Let's make this the best
duel they've ever seen.

144
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:46,540
You're on.

145
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:49,200
But I still wish my Yugipu was here.

146
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,310
Mr.

147
00:07:51,393 --> 00:07:52,840
Moro, you out there?

148
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,320
Hello? Gramps?

149
00:08:07,540 --> 00:08:10,600
Attention, Kybaland
guests. A short, stocky,

150
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,977
elderly gentleman in overalls and a black

151
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:15,884
headband has been separated
from his loved ones.

152
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:20,180
If anyone has lost a grandpa, he's
waiting for you at the main gate.

153
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:22,453
Overalls in a headband?

154
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:23,720
That's my grandpa!

155
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:28,770
Hey, you!

156
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:30,337
Did you hear that announcement?

157
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:32,479
Yeah, and I guess you guys did too.

158
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:33,830
Yep.

159
00:08:33,913 --> 00:08:36,617
And how many elderly gentlemen
with overalls do you guys know?

160
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:37,530
One.

161
00:08:37,613 --> 00:08:40,660
The only problem is he's
not here. Good point.

162
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:43,160
You think we're at the wrong gate?

163
00:08:43,700 --> 00:08:45,360
Hey, check that out.

164
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:47,660
I wonder if Grandpa put it there.

165
00:08:50,800 --> 00:08:51,630
Let's see.

166
00:08:51,713 --> 00:08:53,080
It's some kind of map.

167
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,987
It looks like the whole
layout of Kaiba Land.

168
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,120
And look!

169
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,300
X marks the spot.

170
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:03,238
So you mean if we find that
spot, we'll find Grandpa?

171
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:04,890
I hope.

172
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:07,724
I don't like the looks of this.

173
00:09:08,340 --> 00:09:11,937
Why would Yugi's grandfather pay
just to come here, run and hide,

174
00:09:12,020 --> 00:09:14,597
and then leave us a map
so we can find him, huh?

175
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:15,856
What are you saying?

176
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,420
That someone set a trap for us.

177
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:22,277
Well, I'm not going to fall for any trap.

178
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:25,200
If we want to save
Grandpa, we might have to.

179
00:09:27,100 --> 00:09:31,380
All right, it's time to
begin our semi-final round.

180
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:35,880
Our first duel picks, Sidfrey
Lloyd against Balfrey Ginger.

181
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:40,740
These two daffodans will face off
in Kyber Corp's Galaxy Theater.

182
00:09:43,220 --> 00:09:45,920
And now on to our second matchup,

183
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:50,340
featuring the two youngest minors
to ever join a major tournament,

184
00:09:50,720 --> 00:09:53,317
Rebecca Hawkins and Leon Wilson.

185
00:09:53,400 --> 00:09:57,680
These small fries will wage
war in small town, USA!

186
00:09:59,500 --> 00:10:00,735
Now, do lists, begin!

187
00:10:04,820 --> 00:10:05,840
Let's duel!

188
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,080
Time to duel!

189
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:12,940
Rebecca's got nothing on you!

190
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,780
Scratch this wannabe!

191
00:10:15,160 --> 00:10:18,160
I'll kick things off, if you don't mind.

192
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:22,700
So, the first thing I'll do is
activate my graceful charity!

193
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:30,460
Now I can draw three new cards, and
then I discard two from my hand.

194
00:10:32,560 --> 00:10:35,020
So I'll send these two to the graveyard.

195
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:39,397
And since one of them happens
to be Marie the Fallen One,

196
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,560
I gain an extra 200 life
points with every turn.

197
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:47,640
I'm not done yet.

198
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:50,560
Next I play Fire Princess in attack mode.

199
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:54,737
Then I'll place one card
face down and end my

200
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:58,800
turn I'll start things off
by summoning Forest Wolf

201
00:11:02,340 --> 00:11:07,180
Now attack Rebecca's Fire Princess
With Fairy Tail Fang Attack

202
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,497
What big teeth he has, right?

203
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:21,260
Well, as the fairy tale goes, the better
to devour your princess with, my dear.

204
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:24,020
So, is that the big bad wolf?

205
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:25,240
Wrong story.

206
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:28,180
Now I play a magic card.

207
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:29,980
So go, Curse of Thorns!

208
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:39,380
This stops Marie the Fallen One
from using her special ability.

209
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,660
Not bad, kid. Not bad.

210
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:43,700
Glad you liked it.

211
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:50,500
All right, my move.

212
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:54,080
I summon my bluster dragon in attack mode.

213
00:11:57,260 --> 00:11:58,360
Hey, Leon,

214
00:11:58,760 --> 00:12:03,697
if you think your forest wolf has a big
mouth, then take a close look at my dragons.

215
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:06,660
The better to blast you
back to Fairyland with.

216
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:19,220
When my forest wolf is destroyed,

217
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:22,560
whatever monsters he
swallowed return to the field.

218
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,460
So you got your princess back.

219
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,540
Nice dueling. Thank you.

220
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,195
And there's more where that came from.

221
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,800
Like this direct attack.

222
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,520
That should do for now.

223
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:40,840
Wow, you're just as good
as they say you are.

224
00:12:41,020 --> 00:12:43,817
But if you think that
scares me, you're wrong.

225
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,280
Look out!

226
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:49,109
I'll start by playing Glyph the
Phantom Bird in attack mode.

227
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:52,980
Big deal!

228
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:55,946
As soon as I activate
my face down magic card,

229
00:12:56,100 --> 00:12:58,335
his oversized chicken will be useless!

230
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:07,317
In case you hadn't noticed, when my
Phantom Bird is summoned to the field,

231
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,518
he destroys one of my
opponent's trap or magic cards.

232
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:14,180
And now, Glyph the Phantom
Bird, attack her princess!

233
00:13:22,580 --> 00:13:26,120
Next, I'll activate a magic
card known as Gingerbread House.

234
00:13:26,600 --> 00:13:31,720
And if you think my fairy tale is good
now, just wait till the happy ending.

235
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:34,960
Come on, Rebecca.

236
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:36,597
Let's see what you got.

237
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:38,020
Don't mind if I do.

238
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:39,640
I'll start by...

239
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:42,440
Hey, what's going on?

240
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:51,390
Huh?

241
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:56,420
How strange.

242
00:13:56,780 --> 00:13:59,956
He just raised the attack
points of Rebecca's monster.

243
00:14:00,420 --> 00:14:03,920
It's just like my mom says,
don't fill up on sweets.

244
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:08,917
I know my gingerbread house
seems like a good thing at first,

245
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,380
but once you go inside,

246
00:14:10,660 --> 00:14:12,248
there's a price to be paid.

247
00:14:12,380 --> 00:14:17,940
Sure, you get 600 points, but if your
monster's total is 2,500 or more, boom!

248
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:22,460
It's destroyed, and then I'm
rewarded with 500 extra life points.

249
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:28,080
Leon's cards are so weird, and
I've never seen any of them before!

250
00:14:29,260 --> 00:14:30,280
Enough, gang!

251
00:14:30,700 --> 00:14:32,820
Now I activate the shallow grave!

252
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:34,550
Oh.

253
00:14:34,640 --> 00:14:37,717
So we each choose one
monster to transfer from our

254
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:40,617
graveyard are back to the
field in defense mode.

255
00:14:40,700 --> 00:14:43,600
So how about a warm welcome
for my luster dragon?

256
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:47,400
And let's give it up for the
return of my forest wolf.

257
00:14:49,300 --> 00:14:52,160
Now I'll sacrifice my luster dragon.

258
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:56,680
That lets me summon luster
dragon number two in its place.

259
00:14:59,760 --> 00:15:00,840
Alright, LD.

260
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,937
It's time to show that overgrown
pigeon of his what you've got.

261
00:15:05,020 --> 00:15:06,360
Emerald flame attack.

262
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,800
Had enough yet?

263
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:20,057
Well, I gotta admit, you're
pretty good, Rebecca.

264
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:22,280
But this story is not over yet.

265
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:25,180
So sit back and enjoy!

266
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:28,420
First, I'll switch my
wolf into attack mode.

267
00:15:30,340 --> 00:15:34,634
Then I'll summon a girl you might
remember from your old bedtime stories.

268
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:38,920
And thanks to her fairy godmother,
she'll be able to go to the ball!

269
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:42,060
You guessed it! It's Cinderella!

270
00:15:45,540 --> 00:15:50,420
And her special ability lets me automatically
summon pumpkin carrots to the field!

271
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:54,073
And what princess is complete
without her glass slippers?

272
00:15:56,760 --> 00:15:57,590
Huh?

273
00:15:57,673 --> 00:15:58,720
Give me a break!

274
00:15:59,020 --> 00:15:59,961
Here's the deal.

275
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:02,917
As long as that pumpkin
carriage is on the field,

276
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:08,600
Cinderella is able to bypass your dragon
and attack you directly Now, Cinderella,

277
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:11,154
kick off those slippers and let's party

278
00:16:17,760 --> 00:16:21,677
But Cinderella never takes away
someone's life points without giving

279
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:27,620
something back in return A perfect
fit My dragon's wearing slippers?

280
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:29,070
Yep,

281
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:34,004
and as long as your dragon sports that
stylish footwear, it can attack Cinderella.

282
00:16:34,260 --> 00:16:37,789
Oh, and did I mention your
dragon loses 1,000 attack points?

283
00:16:39,020 --> 00:16:40,140
Is that all?

284
00:16:40,660 --> 00:16:41,490
Nope.

285
00:16:41,573 --> 00:16:44,297
We can't forget about my
wolf in grandma's clothing.

286
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:45,210
Attack!

287
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:58,277
And of course, whenever a monster
wearing glass slippers is destroyed,

288
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:02,617
Cinderella receives a brand new pair
that she can use for her next attack.

289
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:06,100
And the second pair gives
her a 1,000-point boost.

290
00:17:07,900 --> 00:17:11,300
Oh, and last but not
least, one face-down card.

291
00:17:12,180 --> 00:17:16,477
How am I supposed to fight against
Leon's deck of fairy tale rejects?

292
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:17,972
They're driving me nuts!

293
00:17:18,220 --> 00:17:21,985
And I gave up these lame stories
when I threw out my teddy bear!

294
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:23,180
Here goes!

295
00:17:23,680 --> 00:17:24,580
My move!

296
00:17:24,900 --> 00:17:28,959
And I think it's about time one of
us played a real card for a chain!

297
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,340
Tribute to the Doom!

298
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,717
So, who's afraid of the big bad wolf?

299
00:17:32,800 --> 00:17:34,420
Not me, thanks to this!

300
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:41,220
Next, I'll activate the magic
card, Stamping Destruction!

301
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:44,957
It destroys one magic
card on the field and

302
00:17:45,040 --> 00:17:48,100
delivers 500 points of
damage to that card's owner!

303
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:57,840
And finally, I'll give your
princess a royal butt-kicking!

304
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:02,477
Well, not if I can help it!

305
00:18:02,560 --> 00:18:05,380
I activate my Mirror Force Trap Card.

306
00:18:05,600 --> 00:18:08,860
So your attack is deflected
and bounced right back.

307
00:18:12,180 --> 00:18:14,180
No, not him.

308
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:17,040
Fine, your move.

309
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,800
You seem upset. Relax.

310
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:22,774
Dueling is supposed to be fun, Rebecca.

311
00:18:23,140 --> 00:18:24,620
Just look at Cinderella.

312
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:26,256
She's having a ball.

313
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:36,380
I can't believe I'm fighting against
princesses and fairies And losing

314
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:45,697
A victory just wasn't in the
stars for you Here's your winner

315
00:18:45,780 --> 00:18:52,000
The dreading and tasteful
Siegfried Lloyd Come and get me,

316
00:18:52,160 --> 00:18:53,120
Herr Kyloch

317
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,880
I'm on to you, Siegfried.

318
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:06,860
Are you guys sure we're
going the right way?

319
00:19:07,420 --> 00:19:12,244
Assuming we can trust that map, Yugi's
grandpa should be right around that corner.

320
00:19:12,540 --> 00:19:14,080
Let's just hope he's okay.

321
00:19:14,700 --> 00:19:15,740
He better be.

322
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:25,800
That's it He's in a Chinese restaurant?

323
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:31,600
You mean while we were running around like
lunatics, Grandpa was eating wonton soup?

324
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:36,620
Wait, Yugi, be careful

325
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:44,830
Grandpa!

326
00:19:44,913 --> 00:19:46,840
You in there? Hello?

327
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:50,880
No matter what it takes, I'll save you.
